# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored and never committed.
# In the Fly.io cloud deployment these are set with `fly secrets set` instead
# (see README → Deployment); they are read from the environment either way.

# --- Turso (hosted libSQL) database ---
# From `turso db show job-search-agent --url` and `turso db tokens create job-search-agent`.
# Use the libsql:// URL exactly as `turso db show --url` prints it. The
# turso_serverless driver connects over Turso's HTTP API (the managed platform
# does not serve the WebSocket transport), so no scheme change is needed.
# For local dev you may instead point at a throwaway local file, e.g.
#   TURSO_DATABASE_URL=file:dev.db
TURSO_DATABASE_URL=
TURSO_AUTH_TOKEN=

# --- Claude (weekly deep-research sweep, `jsa generate`, `jsa refine`) ---
# Every Claude service drives the Claude Agent SDK. Preferred: a subscription
# OAuth token from `claude setup-token` (usage draws from the plan, not
# per-call billing). Alternative: a pay-as-you-go API key in
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY. Never set both — the CLI prefers ANTHROPIC_API_KEY and
# 401s if that variable holds an OAuth value.
CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# --- Perplexity (the recurring Mon/Wed/Fri Agent API deep research) ---
PERPLEXITY_API_KEY=

# --- Step 5: the Google Sheet application tracker (local only) ---
# The tracker write shells out to the local `gws` CLI, which holds the Google
# OAuth token — that credential stays off the Fly.io server by design, so
# neither of these belongs in `fly secrets`. The spreadsheet id is REQUIRED
# for the Sheet-touching commands (`jsa track`, `jsa generate`, `jsa refetch`'s
# default scope): it is the id of your own tracker Sheet (see README, "Using
# this for your own search") — there is deliberately no default in code. The
# binary defaults to `gws` on PATH.
JSA_TRACKER_SPREADSHEET_ID=
# JSA_GWS_BIN=
